Balancing the Bear Case and Silver Linings

The persistent decline in Swiggy Ltd’s share price reflects a combination of weak profitability, challenging valuation metrics, and bearish technical indicators. The company’s inability to generate positive EBITDA and the poor EBIT to interest coverage ratio underscore financial vulnerabilities that have weighed heavily on investor sentiment. However, the strong quarterly sales growth and rising institutional ownership provide counterpoints that suggest some underlying business momentum remains intact.

This duality creates a complex investment landscape. The stock’s 46% fall from its 52-week high and its underperformance relative to the Sensex and sector peers highlight the severity of the sell-off. Yet, the data also points to pockets of resilience that may warrant closer examination. Buy, sell, or hold at a 52-week low? The complete multi-factor analysis of Swiggy Ltd weighs all these signals.

